# muse doctor/health/wake-guidance checks (#50-honest)

## Goal

Operators can see muse install/delivery/wake state truthfully.
Needs B354 (presence signals known); wake classifier shared with
B356 (env-gated sidecar) — coordinate the enum.

## Contract

- `c2c_doctor_hooks.ml`: `is_muse_registration` triple +
  `check_muse_install` (skill? hooks/plugin? mcpServers entry? —
  presence ONLY, labeled as not-proving-fire per #50) +
  `check_muse_delivery` (DEAF = inbox>0 ∧ ¬poster, kimi
  `classify_kimi_session` pure precedent, if a sidecar exists) +
  wake classifier (`Muse_wake_none | Conditional_monitor`, grok
  `.monitor-locks` pid-check precedent :1166–1301; add a
  `Conditional_env_session_message` arm only if B356 unparks) +
  result field + human/JSON render arms +
  exit-code wiring (DEAF fails); `--rearm` skips confirmed-dead
  (#42) and never mints headless targets (#78).
- `c2c_health_cmd.ml`: probe arm (:208–291 — message MUST contain
  the client name for the `client_status` substring match) +
  `"muse"` in `supported_clients` :564 (B353 may already add it —
  don't duplicate); liveness via `outer_pid_is_ours` (:832–858)
  once managed exists; relay stays grey-when-inactive (B300 —
  via `Relay_activation`, never the public URL).
- `c2c_wake_guidance.ml:29–173`: BOTH contexts (Install +
  Managed_start) with honest class + primary path; unknown-client
  fallback must never be reachable for muse. Delivery vocabulary
  shared with status/instances/doctor (T005 — never overclaim).
- Minor strings (judgment calls, do them): `whoami` recovery hint
  (`c2c_whoami_cmd.ml:42–43`), statusline/inject/deliver-inbox
  `--client` docs, sweep pgrep guard (`c2c_sweep_cmd.ml:267`) if
  managed outer procs match the pattern, `forward-agent-log`
  classifier + path/sniff arms (`c2c_forward_agent_log.ml:421–494`)
  if muse transcripts should be mirrorable.

## Acceptance

- `c2c doctor hooks` + `c2c health` report muse install/delivery/
  wake correctly across: clean, installed-unfired, live, DEAF,
  dead-but-registered states. Every presence check's help/output
  states it does not prove hooks fire (#50).
- Tests: pure classifier matrices (wake + DEAF truth tables),
  doctor-hooks golden tests, wake-guidance arms
  (`test_c2c_wake_guidance.ml`), `test_c2c_doctor_hooks.ml`
  additions; docs-drift clean on new paths/commands.

RESCOPE after B357 merge (parent-review remainder): STRUCK (done by B357): check_muse_install presence set, result field + human/JSON arms, health probe arm, supported_clients. REMAINS: is_muse_registration triple; DEAF classifier (open design: no muse poster exists — likely vacuous or monitor-based, decide + record); wake classifier Muse_wake_none|Conditional_monitor via .monitor-locks pid-check (env arm only if B356 unparks); exit-code wiring + rearm semantics (skip-confirmed-dead/no-mint even if no-op); liveness via outer_pid_is_ours (needs B358 merged); wake-guidance Install+Managed_start arms (B353 NONE stub stands; coordinate with B358 interim arm); minor strings (whoami hint, --client docs, sweep pgrep, forward-agent-log); add explicit does-not-prove-hooks-fire disclaimer to pp_human output. Hold start until B358 merges (shares wake_guidance.ml).